+# Story RC4.2: Reference Panel (Status & Summary)
+
+**Status:** in-progress (briefing pre-approved — epic ACs are canonical)
+**Epic:** RC4 (Landlord Reference Panel & Workflow). Depends on RC4.1 (merged, #604).
+**Model:** `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (briefing policy — execution role).
+**Perkins:** ON.
+**GitHub issue:** #548
+
+## Story
+
+> As a landlord,
+> I want to see each reference's status and read completed summaries with honest framing,
+> So that I always know exactly where things stand — including when a state tells me nothing about the applicant.
+
+RC4.1 shipped the landlord-facing detail payload contract (`reference_calls[]` + `attestation_on_file`).
+RC4.2 **renders** the panel from that contract — the display layer of the reference-checking
+feature: every lifecycle state with §7.4 copy verbatim, the completed-reference summary with
+honest framing ("Not answered", never guessed; "Worth knowing" signals as clues, never
+verdicts), and the expectation-setting explainer. The panel never re-derives state rules
+client-side (AR-RC13 / RC4.1 contract principle). Row ACTIONS (start/skip/take-over/
+correct/substitute) and the attempt-log export are RC4.3/RC4.4 — display-only here.
+
+**The load-bearing rule (honest framing):** a state that tells the landlord nothing about
+the applicant says so — "this tells you nothing about Aisling" — and the summary never
+invents an answer: unanswered verification fields render "Not answered" (never hidden,
+never guessed); `ai_summary` confidence is whatever the server computed (partial caps at
+medium server-side); fraud signals render only when the payload carries them (AD-10 honesty:
+no signal, no invented signal).
+
+## Scope
+
+### OWNS
+1. **`client/src/components/reference_panel.gleam`** (NEW) — the panel card. Renders:
+   - chrome: `bg-white rounded-xl shadow-xl shadow-navy/5 p-6`, heading "Reference Checks ({n})",
+     panel sub-line (§10.3 as amended — pre-trigger: "Starts automatically when you mark the
+     viewing as done." (A5); in flight: "We invite, remind, and nudge — you watch it happen.";
+     all terminal: "All references closed. Summaries and logs stay here."), collapsed-by-default
+     "What this tells you" explainer (§7.8 verbatim), per-user dismissed state.
+   - the Off state (attestation declined): §7.4 verbatim + referee contact chips from the
+     application trios, NO re-ask affordance.
+   - rows per `reference_calls[]`: `refcheck-row-{slot}`, `refcheck-status-{slot}`,
+     `refcheck-expand-{slot}`, `refcheck-overflow-{slot}` testids.
+   - all 12 lifecycle states per §4.2/§7.4: Queued (slate), Invitation sent / Reminder sent /
+     Form opened (navy; mini timeline from the attempts log + what-happens-next), Reference
+     received (teal; expanded-by-default on first view), Partially completed (amber; "answered
+     {m} of {n}" — server-capped confidence), Contact details didn't work (amber),
+     Couldn't be reached (amber), Declined to take part (slate), Declined contact (slate, no
+     route-around suggestion), Skipped by you (slate), Something went wrong (amber, never red).
+   - completed/partial detail: headline pull-quote (amber left border), key-facts definition
+     table ("Not answered" for unanswered), ≤3 notable quotes (from `ai_summary.notable_quotes`
+     when present — v1 deterministic summaries emit none), "Worth knowing" block when ≥1 signal
+     (§7.5 header + per-signal copy verbatim, `border-l-2 border-amber-400`), free-text with
+     the unmoderated-referee-text flag (§9.3), confidence line verbatim
+     ("Confidence: {level} · AI-generated summary — verify before relying on it."),
+     `display_disclaimer` when present.
+   - a11y: `role="region"` + `aria-label="Reference checks"` on the card, rows are buttons
+     with `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls`, status never colour-only.
+2. **`client/src/copy.gleam`** — every panel string (states, explainer, signals, words
+   mapping, free-text flag, export-toast copy not needed in RC4.2). No inline strings in the view.
+3. **`client/src/msg.gleam` + `client/src/model.gleam`** — `UserToggledRefcheckRow(String)`
+   (call id), `UserToggledRefcheckExplainer`, `UserDismissedRefcheckExplainer`; model:
+   `refcheck_expanded: Set(String)`, `refcheck_auto_expanded: Option(String)` (application id
+   that got the first-view auto-expand), `refcheck_explainer_dismissed: Bool` (hydrated from
+   localStorage `rt_refcheck_explainer_dismissed`). Reset on route change (mirror
+   `documents_expanded`).
+4. **`client/src/pages/application_detail.gleam`** — wire the panel into the right column
+   below Applicant Information (both AI and no-AI branches).
+5. **`client/src/client.gleam`** — handlers: row toggle, explainer toggle/dismiss
+   (localStorage write), first-view auto-expand of `form_completed`/`manual_recorded` rows
+   when `ApiReturnedApplicationDetail` lands for an application id != `refcheck_auto_expanded`.
+6. **Contract addition (additive, expand-only):** the RC4.1 payload gains
+   `form_opened_at: Option(String)` (nullable) so the panel can render the "Form opened"
+   state (AC-mandated; the §8.1 contract as merged has no form-open marker — the attempts
+   log records sends only). `shared/reference_call.gleam` (type + encoder + back-compat
+   `optional_field` decoder), `list_reference_calls_for_detail.sql` (COALESCE select),
+   `application_detail_handler.gleam` (map). The RC4.1 strip assertions and wire contract are
+   untouched — additive key only.
+7. **Tests** — `client/test/components/reference_panel_test.gleam` (NEW): the 12-state
+   matrix renders (§4.2 labels verbatim), testids present, expand/collapse toggling, first-view
+   auto-expand, completed detail (key facts with "Not answered", worth-knowing signals,
+   confidence line, unmoderated flag), Off state chips, status-pill colours never red.
+   `shared/test/reference_call_test.gleam`: form_opened_at round-trips (present + absent-key
+   back-compat). `server/test/application/application_detail_handler_test.gleam`: serializer
+   emits form_opened_at.
+
+### Does NOT own (deferred / sibling stories)
+- **Row actions** (start now, skip, re-enable, take over, correct, substitute, retry) — RC4.3.
+  The `⋯` overflow button renders with its testid on rows that will carry actions per §7.3,
+  but is NOT click-wired in RC4.2 (no dead menu, no placeholder items; RC4.3 opens it).
+- **Attempt-log export + notification completeness** — RC4.4 (the mini timeline renders from
+  the attempts log; the full timeline + clipboard export are RC4.4).
+- **"Ask Aisling to nudge"** — RC4.3.
+- **Any server route or state mutation** — none. Display only.
