+## Acceptance Criteria (BDD — from epic RC4.2 + UX §7.1–7.8/§10.3/§13/§9.3 + A5)
+
+**AC1 — Placement & chrome**
+> **Given** the application detail page (v3 layout)
+> **When** the panel renders
+> **Then** it sits in the right column below Applicant Information, above Audit Trail
+> (mobile: immediately after Applicant Information); heading "Reference Checks ({n})";
+> state-tracking sub-line per §10.3 as amended (pre-trigger: "Starts automatically when you
+> mark the viewing as done."); collapsed-by-default "What this tells you" explainer (§7.8
+> verbatim); `data-testid`s `refcheck-card`, `refcheck-row-{slot}`, `refcheck-status-{slot}`,
+> `refcheck-expand-{slot}`, `refcheck-overflow-{slot}` present.
+
+**AC2 — 12-state matrix**
+> **Given** every lifecycle state
+> **When** rows render
+> **Then** state content matches UX §4.2/§7.4 verbatim: Off (declined — referee contact
+> chips, no re-ask affordance), Queued (pre-trigger copy), Invitation sent / Reminder sent /
+> Form opened (mini timeline + what-happens-next), Reference received, Partially completed
+> ("answered {m} of {n}", confidence capped medium — server-side), Contact details didn't
+> work, Couldn't be reached, Declined to take part, Declined contact (no route-around
+> suggestion), Skipped by you, Something went wrong.
+> **And** status-pill colours follow §13 — received teal, waiting/queued slate,
+> reminder/opened navy, needs-attention amber, declined/objected slate — **never red**.
+
+**AC3 — Completed reference detail**
+> **Given** a completed reference, expanded by default on first view
+> **When** the detail renders
+> **Then** headline pull-quote (amber left border), key-facts definition table with
+> "Not answered" for unanswered fields (never hidden, never guessed), ≤3 notable quotes,
+> "Worth knowing" block when ≥1 signal (§7.5 header + per-signal copy verbatim,
+> `border-l-2 border-amber-400`, innocent explanation + suggested action), free-text
+> unmoderated flag (§9.3), confidence line verbatim.
+
+**AC4 — A11y + loading**
+> **Given** the panel loads and is operated by keyboard/screen reader
+> **Then** skeleton shimmer during load (the existing page skeleton covers the detail-load
+> state; the panel itself renders inside `Success`); card `role="region"` with
+> `aria-label="Reference checks"`; rows are buttons with `aria-expanded`/`aria-controls`;
+> status never colour-only.
+
+**AC5 — Data contract discipline**
+> **Given** the payload
+> **When** the panel renders
+> **Then** it renders from `reference_calls[]` + `attestation_on_file` +
+> `reference_contact_choice` only — no client-side state-rule re-derivation; Off ⇔
+> `reference_contact_choice == "declined"`; card hidden for pre-v1 apps (choice NULL) with no
+> rows; pre-trigger (choice attested, no rows) shows sub-line + explainer only.
